  "design_purpose": "Every modifier attaches to tags, never to a skill or a socket (D-014). applies_to ['self'] marks a character stat; anything else names the skill tags the modifier excites. effect keys follow the resolver's increased-vs-more rule: add_* is flat, increased_* sums within its bucket, more_* multiplies. A base's allowed_modifier_tags is the roll pool - specific tags, never the generic offence/defence pair alone, so a sceptre cannot grow physical mods and a mace cannot grow cold ones; rarity is a modifier count (plain 0, keen 1-2, wrought 3-4) and never a stat. Uniques (hand-authored, rule-bending) are the next slice."
}
